{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Collective Ops From Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Mesh` class that wires N `multiprocessing.Queue` instances into a ring and exposes `send(dst, tensor)` and `recv(src)` per rank."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `ring_allreduce(mesh, rank, world_size, tensor)` running the two-pass algorithm."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `broadcast(mesh, rank, world_size, tensor, src)` over a logarithmic tree."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `allgather(mesh, rank, world_size, tensor)` using N-1 rotations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `reduce_scatter(mesh, rank, world_size, tensor)` as the first half of allreduce."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `_gloo_reference(op, world_size, tensor)` that runs the same input through `torch.distributed` with gloo for byte-equal comparison."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: per-primitive verification table comparing queue-mesh and gloo outputs, followed by a per-rank byte counter that proves the 2T(N-1)/N scaling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a tree allreduce variant and switch between ring and tree by message size. Measure the crossover.\n2. Add a `recv_timeout_ms` so a stalled rank surfaces a deadline error instead of hanging forever.\n3. Replace `multiprocessing.Queue` with TCP sockets for the four primitives. Same tests, real wire.\n4. Add a bandwidth instrumentation hook so the per-rank byte counter logs to JSONL.\n5. Compare wall-clock time of ring versus tree on 4 ranks for tensors of size 1KB, 1MB, 16MB. Defend the crossover empirically."
      ]
    }
  ],
